WEBVTT

00:04:58.468 --> 00:05:01.967
and questions more than statements
when it involves the other person.

00:05:02.533 --> 00:05:03.919
When discussing intimacy,

00:05:03.943 --> 00:05:06.534
check-ins like "Does that feel good?

00:05:06.558 --> 00:05:08.010
Do you like that?"

00:05:08.034 --> 00:05:12.327
in addition to letting your partner
know what you need, want and like,

00:05:12.351 --> 00:05:15.617
helps us have experiences
we remember fondly

00:05:15.641 --> 00:05:17.221
and have no regrets about.

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:21.117
We need to broaden
our understanding of consent

00:05:21.141 --> 00:05:22.945
and start thinking of it as a verb,

00:05:22.969 --> 00:05:24.119
not a noun.

00:05:24.464 --> 00:05:28.103
To consent is an active,
ongoing agreement,

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:30.195
not a checkbox to be ticked.